# Rust build output for the wasm extension. `Cargo.lock` is committed on
# purpose: this is an application-like cdylib, and pinning the
# `zed_extension_api` version keeps Zed's wasm build reproducible.
/target

# Build artifacts. When this directory is installed as a dev extension, Zed
# compiles `extension.wasm` here and clones + compiles each grammar into
# `grammars/<name>/` and `grammars/<name>.wasm`. They are outputs, not sources:
# the grammar sources live in `editors/tree-sitter-fx` and
# `editors/tree-sitter-fxc`.
/extension.wasm
/grammars/
